///! The Cryo runtime: what a compiled program calls that the language itself
///! does not define - the program entry, the panic machinery and the check
///! handlers, the freestanding allocator and backtrace (see
///! `abi/lang_items.def` for every symbol and which build defines it).
///!
///! One project, built once per configuration into one `libcryort.a`:
///!
///!   - freestanding (`--no-runtime`): no libc; the entry, the allocator and
///!     the backtrace are the runtime's own, output and exit are raw OS calls,
///!     and a panic aborts.
///!   - hosted, abort (`--panic=abort`): linked beside libc; a panic reports and
///!     ends the process through libc `exit`, so buffered stdio is flushed.
///!   - hosted, unwind (`--panic=unwind`): a panic unwinds the stack, running
///!     each frame's drops, until a `catch_unwind` or the root catch stops it.
///!
///! A configuration is chosen by the build's own options, which the
///! declarations here are gated on (`no_runtime`, `panic_unwind`): the panic
///! implementation a build defines is the strategy it is compiled with.  The
///! compiler builds the configuration a program links on first use, with
///! itself, and keeps it beside these sources (`.bin/<triple>/<configuration>/`).

namespace CryoRt;

/// Output, formatting and termination primitives every other module uses.
module Sys;

/// The program entry.
module Core;

/// The panic funnel and the check handlers, one implementation per strategy.
module Panic;

/// The freestanding global allocator.
module Alloc;

/// The freestanding stack backtrace.
module Backtrace;
